    "before": "extra-large",
    "after": "extra-large"
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "hotspots",
   "header": "<h2> Logging and Networking Your Data </h2>",
   "intro": "",
   "img": {
    "src": "/fileadmin/_processed_/a/1/csm_vernetzung_infodots_11_bae0da944d.webp",
    "alt": "",
    "w": 1340,
    "h": 852
   },
   "spots": [
    {
     "x": 53.7,
     "y": 34.748,
     "label": "Contour Correction",
     "text": "<h3>Contour Correction</h3> <h4>Contour Correction for Molding Tools</h4> <p>Contour correction for molding tools – Nominal/actual comparison of the scanned contour with the nominal contour in DXF format. The »»coCon«« software inverts the deviations and generates a contour correction, which is transferred to the machine as a new DXF file.</p>"
    },
    {
     "x": 76.3,
     "y": 27.516,
     "label": "Interfaces",
     "text": "<h3>Interfaces</h3> <h4>Interfaces</h4> <p>Interfaces – the measuring machine receives a measurement data file from the programming system or the grinding machine and automatically generates the measurement sequence. The measured actual tool data is transferred from the ZOLLER inspection and measuring machine to the programming system or the machine control, where the NC program is optimized for high volume manufacturing.</p>"
    }
   ],
